  "caveats": [
    "The test set was inspected during RF3 development and again during S4 development, so all RF3/RF4 test comparisons are exploratory.",
    "The old smoke and paper protocols overlapped; they were not independent confirmations.",
    "The balanced 50 percent test attack prevalence does not represent typical deployment prevalence.",
    "The witness substring is an automated proxy rather than a human-confirmed attack-success label.",
    "Only one model, fixed system prompt, seed, and decoding configuration were evaluated.",
    "No confidence interval or paired significance result currently establishes the S4 improvement.",
    "S4 requires logits and an additional forward pass.",
    "Detection occurs after generation and cannot undo generation-time side effects.",
    "Random-forest impurity importance is descriptive and not causal.",
    "Historical package, model-revision, accelerator, and dataset hashes were not completely recorded."
  ]
